MASTER PROMPT — TRON BIKE

A Semi-3D, 5-Player Online Multiplayer Light Cycle Game

Build a complete, polished, mobile-first online multiplayer TRON-inspired light-cycle game as an installable Progressive Web App (PWA).

The game must deliver a premium futuristic arcade experience inspired by the classic TRON light-cycle concept, with enormous open-world arena gameplay, glowing neon trails, semi-3D graphics, smooth bike movement, real-time multiplayer, player accounts, friends, private rooms and cinematic victory sequences.

IMPORTANT: This is a complete game development specification. Implement the actual working game, not just a visual prototype, mockup, landing page or collection of non-functional screens.

Do not omit features, replace real multiplayer with simulated multiplayer, or simplify the game into a small arena.

---

1. CORE GAME CONCEPT

The game is a last-player-standing TRON light-cycle battle.

- Support up to 5 real human players in one online match.
- Minimum 2 players to start a match.
- Every player controls a futuristic neon motorcycle.
- Bikes automatically move forward continuously.
- Players can only turn left or right.
- Every bike leaves a permanent glowing vertical light wall/trail behind it while alive.
- Players must avoid colliding with any active light trail and the outer arena boundary.
- The last surviving player wins.
- There is absolutely no match time limit.
- Matches continue for as long as necessary until a winner is determined.

The game should feel exciting, competitive, smooth and visually impressive.

2. MOBILE-ONLY REQUIREMENT

The game is designed exclusively for mobile phones.

- Mobile-first interface and gameplay.
- Support different mobile screen sizes and aspect ratios.
- Landscape orientation is mandatory.
- Use landscape orientation locking where supported by the browser and PWA.
- If the player opens the game in portrait mode, display a full-screen rotate-your-phone message.
- Do not allow normal gameplay in portrait mode.
- The interface, HUD, camera controls and touch gestures must be optimized for landscape screens.
- Prevent accidental browser scrolling, zooming, pull-to-refresh and unwanted touch gestures during gameplay.
- Maintain smooth performance on reasonably capable Android and iOS phones.

Do not create a desktop-oriented game interface and simply shrink it for mobile.

