31. IMPORTANT GAMEPLAY EDGE CASES

Handle these cases properly:

- Two players hit each other's trails simultaneously.
- Multiple players are eliminated in one collision event.
- A player hits their own trail.
- A player reaches the outer energy wall.
- A player disconnects during gameplay.
- A player reconnects after elimination.
- A player disconnects during the countdown.
- The host disconnects.
- A player attempts to join after the match starts.
- A player attempts to move before GO.
- A bike turns too quickly or attempts an impossible reversal.
- A bike moves at high speed near a trail.
- An eliminated player's trail must disappear.
- A spectator attempts to control a living bike.
- A player attempts to trigger a fake victory.
- Two simultaneous match-ending events occur.
- All players are eliminated simultaneously.
- Players request a rematch at different times.

Never allow these situations to break the match.

